-WimFile "I:\images\Win11_Enterprise.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "I:\configs\unattend.xml" -DataDiskNumber 1 -EnableBitLocker -BitLockerPin "ReplaceWithYourPin42" -Force -Silent

:: ============================================================================
:: IMPORTANT: startnet.cmd reads ONLY THE FIRST LINE of this file (via `set /p`).
:: Everything below this banner is reference documentation — `::` lines are
:: ignored. Edit line 1 above to match your USB.
:: ============================================================================
::
:: Line 1 above is the **two-partition USB** pattern (FAT32 WinPE boot
:: partition + NTFS IMAGES data partition). I: is an example - whatever drive
:: letter the IMAGES partition gets is fine, just keep the paths consistent.
::
:: ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
:: Alternative pattern A: single-ISO workflow (build_iso.ps1 output - one
:: file, Rufus to USB). {DRIVE} is substituted at boot time with the actual
:: drive letter WinPE assigns the USB. build_iso.ps1 writes this file
:: automatically; edit before running the builder if needed.
::
::     -WimFile "{DRIVE}\images\Win11_Pro_Custom.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "{DRIVE}\configs\unattend.xml" -Force -Silent
::
:: ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
:: Alternative pattern B: interactive / TUI variant - pre-locates the WIM dir
:: but prompts the operator for edition selection, target disk, and
:: confirmations. Good for lab / testing USBs.
::
::     -ImagePath "{DRIVE}\images"
